1. ⁠What in Pod Disruption Budget (PDB) in K8s
ANS : A PDB defines how many pods of a replicated application can be unavailable during voluntary disruptions
      (e.g., node drain, cluster upgrade, or maintenance).
       It helps maintain application availability while performing operations that might evict pods.
   It does not prevent involuntary disruptions (like node crashes).
------------------------------------------------------------
when to use RollingUpdate and PDB.
Use **RollingUpdate** for **app version upgrades** to control pod rollout, and use a **Pod Disruption Budget (PDB)** to
**protect availability during cluster-level operations** like node upgrades, autoscaling, or preemptions.
| Use Case               | Use RollingUpdate | Use PDB      |
| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ------------ |
| App version upgrade    | ✅ Yes             | ❌ Not needed |
| Node upgrade (`drain`) | ❌ No              | ✅ Yes        |
| Cluster autoscaling    | ❌ No              | ✅ Yes        |
| Pod preemption         | ❌ No              | ✅ Yes        |
