Q. What are the services? Explain different types of services in Kubernetes?
ANS : 
 Kubernetes services enables communication between various components within or outside the application
     1.  cluster ip: Facilitates internal communication with other apps in your cluster, no external access and its the 
        default Kubernetes service.
     2. Node Port: Open a specific port on the node and forward traffic to pod via the service, port to choose from 30000:32767
     3.  Load Balancer: Load Balancer, which will route the traffic from the external to the service. 
        standard way to expose your application to the internet 
